{"task":"transcribe","language":"English","duration":101.447368704,"text":" GiveProperties tracks rent, arrears, and utilities. Two weekly automations split the work. The updater records rent payments, rolls arrears forward, and refreshes utility readings and tenant status. The verifier audits the workbook for missing or duplicate rent, balances that don't reconcile, stale readings, and missing lease data, and flags what's wrong without touching the data. One keeps it current. The other keeps it trustworthy. GAK Properties goes a step further. Every Friday, the verifier reads all 15 tabs of the workbook, plus tenant notices, utility bills, QuickBooks statements, and bank alerts from a dedicated inbox, and emails a numbered list of findings, proposals, conflicts, and notices. A reply drives the updater. Yes, as the figure, correct, writes the fixed value, okay, just acknowledges. Every write is deduplicated, cross-checked, logged with evidence, and locked to GAC, so it can never touch GIF. For Noor Hammam, a SPA, a daily task acts as the registrar for the operations workbook. It reads six tabs, register, people, decisions, gates, money, and the change lock. It only writes what a source supports, and every change cell is logged with its old value, new value, and evidence. When something is missing or contradictory, it doesn't guess. It marks it needs ruling. On the owner's dashboard, Refresh Data pulls all six tabs live and remaps every task to its current row. So edits land in the right place. Refresh, review, edit.","words":[{"word":"GiveProperties","start":0.16,"end":0.88},{"word":"tracks","start":0.88,"end":1.3},{"word":"rent,","start":1.3,"end":2.34},{"word":"arrears,","start":2.34,"end":2.68},{"word":"and","start":2.68,"end":3.24},{"word":"utilities.","start":3.24,"end":4.24},{"word":"Two","start":4.46,"end":4.62},{"word":"weekly","start":4.62,"end":5.1},{"word":"automations","start":5.1,"end":5.72},{"word":"split","start":5.72,"end":6.08},{"word":"the","start":